The image displays confocal microscopy of muscle injection sites over time (6h to Day 7) after intramuscular injection of Alexa Fluor 647-labeled Nano-11 (red) and ovalbumin (green). Stained for cell nuclei (blue) and various immune cell markers (MHCII, Ly6C, Mac-2, 1A8), these images illustrate Nano-11's ability to induce a transient inflammatory response. The nanoparticles are visibly taken up by recruited cells, primarily Mac-2+ macrophages and MHCII+ antigen-presenting cells, indicating their active involvement in the immune response at the injection site.